  abstract = {This study examines whether people's cultural tastes are affected by the provision of categorical (eg, genre) information of the cultural objects being evaluated, and whether this effect differs by a person's educational attainment. Specifically, this study tests the hypotheses, suggested by a previous exploratory study, that the tastes of high-education people become more lenient (eg, favorable) when genre categories are salient, while the taste of low-education people become more restrictive (eg, unfavorable) when genre category information is salient.}
